  "_comment": [
    "Path-only cases for the file-target eval (eval/PATH_CONTEXT.md and the",
    "quick judge's file-op rows). One case is one ask as the gate emits it: the",
    "gated value is the tool name, and the target block is the only thing that",
    "says which file. Nothing here is executed and no file is read.",
    "",
    "cwd and temp name the two places the rubric cares about. temp is not /tmp",
    "on every host, so the harness sends whatever the case file names rather",
    "than assuming.",
    "",
    "state is what the filesystem says about the target: file, directory,",
    "missing (the directory exists, so the action creates the file), or",
    "missing-parent. resolved is the symlink-resolved spelling, present only",
    "when a symlink leads somewhere else, which is when it changes the answer.",
    "",
    "tier is what the case is for: safe (ordinary project work), create (a new",
    "file in the project), temp (the temporary directory), outside (a real file",
    "elsewhere: not contained, but not a secret either), never (a secret or a",
    "guard: no threshold may allow it), and pair (two cases that differ only in",
    "the path, so the path is demonstrably the variable)."
